WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:08.184
Mother Teresa by Darcy Adrian Valance Penguin readers level one.

00:00:08.244 --> 00:00:14.576
There are a lot of good people in the world, but not many of them are world famous.

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:18.878
Mother Teresa was a small quiet nun.

00:00:18.938 --> 00:00:26.122
She died in 1997 in India, but people in many countries remember her.

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:29.594
They talk about her and they love her.

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:31.090
Why?

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.268
Read her story.

00:00:33.328 --> 00:00:36.219
The answer is here.

00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:39.610
Agnes Goncha.

00:00:39.671 --> 00:00:44.473
For her 15 years, her name was not Theresa.

00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:46.494
It was Agnes.

00:00:46.554 --> 00:00:50.156
Her family name was Boyaggio.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.757
There were two children in the family before her.

00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.300
A boy and a girl.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:03.982
Then little Agnes Gonsha came into the world on the 26th of August 1910.

00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:10.984
Her mother and father were from Albania, but they lived in the turn of Skopia.

00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:15.235
At that time, Skopia was in Serbia.

00:01:15.295 --> 00:01:20.616
They had a good home because her father did well in his work.

00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:24.048
Then her father suddenly died.

00:01:24.108 --> 00:01:31.275
Agnes was only eight years old Her sister was 14 and her brother was 11.

00:01:31.335 --> 00:01:37.290
Things were difficult for Agnes' mother, but she was strong for her children.

00:01:37.349 --> 00:01:39.762
She worked and did well.

00:01:39.822 --> 00:01:44.366
She loved the children and they had a happy home.

00:01:44.426 --> 00:01:47.878
There were some poor people near their home.

00:01:47.938 --> 00:01:54.444
These people did not have much money for food and Agnes' mother was good to them too.

00:01:54.504 --> 00:02:01.000
She was a Christian, a Catholic and God was very important to her.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:08.136
She prayed to God every evening with her children and they all went to church every week.

00:02:08.196 --> 00:02:15.572
At the church, there were stories about Christian missionaries in India and poor African countries.

00:02:15.632 --> 00:02:18.354
These people lived for God.

00:02:18.414 --> 00:02:27.262
They went to India and Africa because they wanted to bring God's love to poor people there.

00:02:27.322 --> 00:02:33.484
Agnes loved hearing about the work of these missionaries.

00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:38.156
She started to think, what am I going to do for God?

00:02:38.216 --> 00:02:42.087
She wanted to live for God, but how?

00:02:42.147 --> 00:02:44.558
Did she want to be a nun?

00:02:44.618 --> 00:02:47.699
Did she want to live only for God?

00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:50.570
She prayed for answers.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:54.801
After five years, the answer came to her.

00:02:54.861 --> 00:02:57.815
She wanted to live only for him.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:03:01.309
She wanted to be a nun in India.

00:03:01.369 --> 00:03:04.480
Her mother was very unhappy about this.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.002
She loved her daughter and did not want to say goodbye to her.

00:03:09.062 --> 00:03:13.243
She went to her bedroom and stayed there all day.

00:03:13.303 --> 00:03:23.176
But after a day and a night, she came out and said to Agnes, put your hand in his hand and walk with him.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:32.122
On the 25th of September, 1928, Agnes said goodbye to her friends and her home in Scopia.

00:03:32.182 --> 00:03:36.344
At the station she said goodbye to her family.

00:03:36.404 --> 00:03:42.260
She was 18 years old and she did not see her mother or her sister again.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:50.296
2 India She went by train and boat to Ireland.

00:03:50.356 --> 00:03:53.906
There she went to the home of the Loreto nuns.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:59.756
She wanted to be a Loreto nun because many of them worked in India.

00:03:59.816 --> 00:04:05.538
Agnes stayed with the nuns at Loreto House in Dublin for six weeks.

00:04:05.598 --> 00:04:09.870
Then she was on a boat again to India.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.450
She was now Sister Theresa.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.663
These days, you can get from Ireland to India very quickly.

00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:23.517
But in those days, people were on the boat for seven weeks.

00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:37.062
It went from Ireland to Spain, then across the Mediterranean Sea to Suez in Egypt, down the Red Sea, across the Arabian Sea to Sri Lanka, and then up to Calcutta in India.

00:04:37.122 --> 00:04:41.913
From Calcutta, she went by train to Darjeeling.

00:04:41.973 --> 00:04:49.779
Calcutta was a big place with a lot of noise, but Darjeeling was quiet and beautiful.

00:04:49.839 --> 00:04:57.208
Young sister Theresa did not know much English but she was a good student.

00:04:57.268 --> 00:05:01.572
She was friendly too and she often smiled.

00:05:01.632 --> 00:05:04.454
She was very happy there.

00:05:04.514 --> 00:05:12.901
After two years her English was good and she started to teach children in the Nuns school.

00:05:12.961 --> 00:05:17.946
Then she moved to one of the Loreto Nuns schools in Calcutta.

00:05:18.006 --> 00:05:23.509
Its name was Loreto and Tally, a big school for girls.

00:05:23.569 --> 00:05:27.540
Many of the girls were from poor families.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:34.313
The school day started early in the morning, but the Nuns day started before that.

00:05:34.373 --> 00:05:38.314
Every morning, the Nuns prayed for a long time.

00:05:38.374 --> 00:05:42.276
Then they worked in the school in the morning and the afternoon.

00:05:42.336 --> 00:05:48.576
They worked in the evening too, because many of the girls lived at the school.

00:05:48.636 --> 00:05:53.204
They prayed again and then went to bed.

00:05:53.264 --> 00:05:56.266
The nuns did not have holidays.

00:05:56.326 --> 00:05:59.939
They did not listen to music or go shopping.

00:05:59.998 --> 00:06:02.630
They did not see their families.

00:06:02.689 --> 00:06:06.532
But they were happy because they lived for God.

00:06:06.592 --> 00:06:13.156
They were happy and strong all day because they remembered his love every morning.

00:06:13.216 --> 00:06:18.456
Sister Teresa liked teaching and she was good at it.

00:06:18.516 --> 00:06:29.408
She was a teacher at Loretta Intalli for 12 years and then from 1944 she was the head teacher for four years.

00:06:29.468 --> 00:06:39.462
The Streets of Calcutta Calcutta or Calcutta today has 15 million people.

00:06:39.522 --> 00:06:47.388
In the 1940s it was a very big place too and many new people arrived every year.

00:06:47.448 --> 00:06:54.203
The people were Hindus, Muslims, Christians, Sikhs and Buddhists.

00:06:54.263 --> 00:07:01.316
Calcutta had beautiful buildings, big hotels, offices, banks and houses.

00:07:01.376 --> 00:07:05.068
Many writers and famous people lived there.

00:07:05.128 --> 00:07:08.480
But Calcutta had some big problems.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.362
A lot of people were very poor.

00:07:11.422 --> 00:07:18.154
They did not have any money and they lived in slums, bad places with bad houses.

00:07:18.214 --> 00:07:21.296
Many people did not have a home.

00:07:21.356 --> 00:07:24.318
They lived and died in the streets.

00:07:24.378 --> 00:07:30.833
The years 1943 to 46 were very bad years for Calcutta.

00:07:30.893 --> 00:07:35.396
There was not much food and it was very expensive.

00:07:35.456 --> 00:07:44.754
Poor families did not have money for this expensive food and in those three years about 3 million people died.

00:07:44.814 --> 00:07:49.044
Every day there were dead people in the streets.

00:07:49.104 --> 00:07:55.906
Mother Teresa wanted to help the poor people in the slums, but this was difficult for her.

00:07:55.965 --> 00:08:00.868
She was a nun, and nuns did not often go out into the streets.

00:08:00.928 --> 00:08:12.016
Many nuns helped poor people in schools, big food kitchens and hospitals, but nuns did not usually go out to poor people in slums.

00:08:12.076 --> 00:08:16.545
She prayed to God for an answer to her problem.

00:08:16.605 --> 00:08:25.996
On the 10th of September, 1946, she was on a train from Calcutta to Darjeeling, and the answer came to her.

00:08:26.056 --> 00:08:32.068
The answer was, go and work in the slums with the poor people.

00:08:32.129 --> 00:08:39.402
This was new work for a nun, and the head of the Catholic Church in Calcutta said, wait.

00:08:39.462 --> 00:08:42.613
He wanted to think about it first.

00:08:42.674 --> 00:08:45.930
Mother Theresa wanted to start quickly.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.516
but she waited two years.

00:08:48.576 --> 00:08:53.068
Then in August 1948, a letter came from him.

00:08:53.128 --> 00:08:56.710
He was happy about her new work.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:09:08.144
Loreto Antaly was her home and the nuns were her only friends, but she said goodbye and moved into a small room near a slum.

00:09:08.204 --> 00:09:22.330
The Blue and White Sarri Indian women usually dress in Sarri's There are beautiful, expensive saris, and there are poor saris for poor women.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:29.636
Mother Teresa dressed in a poor blue and white sari because she wanted to work with very poor people.

00:09:29.696 --> 00:09:39.372
Today, there are many nuns in these blue and white saris, but on her first day in the slum, Mother Teresa was alone.

00:09:39.432 --> 00:09:45.614
She was only one small woman with no helpers and no money.

00:09:45.675 --> 00:09:49.004
How did she start her new work?

00:09:49.064 --> 00:09:54.326
First, she prayed to God, and then she walked into the Slum.

00:09:54.386 --> 00:09:57.376
There she talked to poor children.

00:09:57.436 --> 00:09:59.887
Many of them lived in the street.

00:09:59.947 --> 00:10:05.448
They had no home, no family, and no school.

00:10:05.508 --> 00:10:08.939
She started to teach them in the street.

00:10:08.999 --> 00:10:10.769
The children liked her.

00:10:10.829 --> 00:10:15.661
And the day after that, a lot of children came to her new school.

00:10:15.721 --> 00:10:18.603
then they came every day.

00:10:18.664 --> 00:10:23.016
One day there was a poor old woman in the street.

00:10:23.076 --> 00:10:27.168
She did not have a home and she was very ill.

00:10:27.228 --> 00:10:32.882
The doctors in the hospital did not want her because she was poor and very old.

00:10:32.942 --> 00:10:35.063
She was a dying woman.

00:10:35.123 --> 00:10:37.344
She did not have a family.

00:10:37.404 --> 00:10:39.086
She was alone.

00:10:39.146 --> 00:10:42.610
People in the street did not want to go near her.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:46.476
But Mother Teresa went to her and talked to her.

00:10:46.536 --> 00:10:49.348
She washed the woman and stayed with her.

00:10:49.408 --> 00:10:53.482
The woman died, but she did not die alone.

00:10:53.542 --> 00:10:58.516
She died with a friend, with her hand in Mother Teresa's hand.

00:10:58.576 --> 00:11:01.908
There were often dying people in those streets.

00:11:01.968 --> 00:11:06.963
Mother Teresa stayed with them, and they did not die alone.

00:11:07.023 --> 00:11:14.692
Many poor street people did not have any food, Mother Teresa asked people for food for them.

00:11:14.752 --> 00:11:16.934
Some people helped her.

00:11:16.994 --> 00:11:20.798
Some people were angry and did not help.

00:11:20.858 --> 00:11:24.801
For two months, Mother Teresa worked alone.

00:11:24.861 --> 00:11:27.814
It was a difficult time for her.

00:11:27.874 --> 00:11:33.928
Then two of her Indian students from Loretta and Tally came to her and worked with her.

00:11:33.988 --> 00:11:38.115
After two years, there were 12 nuns with her.

00:11:38.175 --> 00:11:45.030
They all had blue and white saris, and they had a name, the missionaries of charity.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:49.811
They worked in street schools and the open street clinics.

00:11:49.871 --> 00:11:56.453
These clinics were not hospitals, but they were a big help for people in the slums.

00:11:56.513 --> 00:12:02.885
People in Calcutta started to talk about Mother Theresa and her missionaries of charity.

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:07.736
Many people wanted to help her and to give money to her.

00:12:07.796 --> 00:12:17.420
In 1952, the government of Calcutta gave her a big building and she started a home for dying people there.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:22.223
After this, the nuns started a big home for children.

00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:28.356
Many poor children in Calcutta did not have a home or a mother or father.

00:12:28.416 --> 00:12:35.115
At the nuns' new children's home, there was food and a bed for them and love too.

00:12:35.175 --> 00:12:42.404
For 10 years, Mother Teresa and her missionaries of charity worked only in Calcutta.

00:12:42.464 --> 00:12:45.796
Every year, there were new nuns.

00:12:45.856 --> 00:12:50.810
After 10 years, they started to work away from Calcutta too.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:13:01.237
They opened new homes for dying people, homes for children, schools, clinics and food kitchens in 23 places in India.

00:13:01.297 --> 00:13:04.818
A love letter to the world.

00:13:04.878 --> 00:13:08.528
There are poor people in every country.

00:13:08.588 --> 00:13:15.700
In 1965, the missionaries of charity started working in Venezuela, South America.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:19.281
After that, they opened a home in Rome.

00:13:19.342 --> 00:13:26.034
Then they went to Tanzania and many countries in Africa, Europe and Asia.

00:13:26.094 --> 00:13:33.364
In 1969, there was a television program about Mother Teresa and her work.

00:13:33.424 --> 00:13:38.626
It was a BBC programme and it was on British TV first.

00:13:38.686 --> 00:13:43.190
After the programme, many letters arrived for her.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.775
A lot of people wanted to work with her or give money.

00:13:47.835 --> 00:13:52.740
Then people in Europe, the US and Asia watch the programme.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:56.102
People in many countries wanted to help her.

00:13:56.162 --> 00:14:00.770
Suddenly Mother Theresa was world famous.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:03.916
She did not like being famous.

00:14:03.976 --> 00:14:06.958
The missionaries of charity were not hers.

00:14:07.018 --> 00:14:08.480
They were gods.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.674
She was only a pen in God's hand, she often said.

00:14:12.734 --> 00:14:16.397
And she is sending a love letter to the world.

00:14:16.457 --> 00:14:19.660
People often asked her about her work.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:26.075
One question was, you are with ill people and dying people every day.

00:14:26.136 --> 00:14:27.706
Is it difficult?

00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:29.548
How do you do it?

00:14:29.608 --> 00:14:34.682
Her answer was, I see God in every person.

00:14:34.743 --> 00:14:39.776
For Mother Teresa, love of God was the important thing.

00:14:39.836 --> 00:14:43.998
She wanted to give her love to God, but we cannot see God.

00:14:44.058 --> 00:14:46.660
We can only see God in people.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:51.964
She loved poor people and dying people because she loved God in them.

00:14:52.024 --> 00:14:56.836
For her, this was beautiful, not difficult.

00:14:56.896 --> 00:15:04.440
She was on television again in 1979 because the Nobel Peace Prize went to her.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.632
This famous prize was $150,000 in that year.

00:15:09.692 --> 00:15:11.974
A lot of money then.

00:15:12.034 --> 00:15:17.316
Every year the prize goes to an important worker for world peace.

00:15:17.376 --> 00:15:22.928
Many important people go to Oslo from many countries for the prize day.

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:30.950
On that day in 1979, Mother Theresa talked to them about love and peace.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:34.974
They asked her, how can we get world peace?

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:40.468
She answered, go home and love your family.

00:15:40.528 --> 00:15:46.954
In the 1980s, there were missionaries of charity in a hundred countries.

00:15:47.014 --> 00:15:53.485
They were not only in poor countries, there was a home for dying people in New York too.

00:15:53.545 --> 00:16:02.546
Mother Teresa often talked to heads of government in these countries, but she always dressed in her poor woman's sari.

00:16:02.606 --> 00:16:09.941
In 1990, Mother Teresa was 80 years old, but she did not start working.

00:16:10.001 --> 00:16:13.323
Her day started at four o'clock in the morning.

00:16:13.383 --> 00:16:16.274
She worked all day and into the night.

00:16:16.334 --> 00:16:19.026
She had little sleep.

00:16:19.086 --> 00:16:23.110
A light in a dark time.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:31.948
Mother Teresa died in September 1997 at the home of the missionaries of charity in Calcutta.

00:16:32.008 --> 00:16:41.946
At that time, there were 4,000 missionaries of charity in 123 countries and 3 million people worked with them.

00:16:42.006 --> 00:16:46.388
People wanted to see her and say goodbye to her.

00:16:46.449 --> 00:16:51.700
Poor people from Calcutta and people from the government of India came.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.732
important people arrived from many countries.

00:16:55.792 --> 00:17:02.379
One person said about her, she was a light in a dark time.

00:17:02.439 --> 00:17:12.050
Mother Teresa was a light for the poor people of Calcutta, but she is a light for all of us too, in every country of the world.

